{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-17T18:28:32.192Z","author":"pi-glm","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"grok-4.7","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"112d48127ede778beff721ba","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"grok-4.7","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Node 22 default reporter emits name: UnitRefusal and error: Unit dimensions differ. Node 26 spec reporter emits UnitRefusal: Unit dimensions differ. The classifier must accept both and still reject syntax and load failures."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-unit-wasm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Node 22 revert proof misses TAP UnitRefusal failures"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"test/revert.acceptance.ts treats a safeguard removal as behavioral only when the child output matches AssertionError, a missing expected rejection, or UnitRefusal followed by a colon. Node 22's test runner prints the refusal as TAP fields name and error, so the same behavioral failure is rejected and the release gate stays red."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["ci","tests"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-17T18:28:32.192Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-17T18:28:32.192Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"pi-glm"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"On Node 22, run npm run test:revert. The context-compatibility removal is the failing case."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A behavioral UnitRefusal on Node 22 and Node 26 is classified as behavioral. Syntax errors and module load errors are still rejected."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Node 22 prints not ok for comparison refuses dimensions kinds subjects populations digests and windows, and that output does not match the colon-suffixed UnitRefusal pattern. Node 26 passes."}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"4efb3924bfa8c359d57488e3a25f6b67c5d53a6f6d1457481b97078a7cb75a0b","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Record the Node 22 revert classification defect","event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"6ff232f2affc100845f98999a6c56d4364f927e3d19a4f452ebffed52574900f"}
